  "safe_special_filter_lemma": {
    "consequence": "Only special-meeting branch blocker rows are filtered to orders four and five. Isolate-only rows are never filtered before the two branches are coupled.",
    "proof": "The row r hits its own branch by definition and the opposite branch because every opposite complement contains both branch specials. For each v in r, branch minimality supplies a branch triple disjoint from r without v; adjoining the opposite two-set remains disjoint because r contains none of those vertices. Thus every deletion of v fails globally.",
    "statement": "If r is a minimal transversal of one branch triple clutter and r meets a special of that branch, then r is a minimal transversal of the full coupled facet-complement clutter."
  },
